        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right shin wound and reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Patient reports a right shin wound after knocking it on a metal platform at work approximately 7 days ago. Over the last 3–4 days, redness, tenderness, and yellow ooze have increased. Reports feeling off, increased tiredness, and a mild limp due to pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Right anterior shin wound examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "effectiveDateTime": "2025-11-22",
        "valueString": "Superficial laceration approximately 2.5 cm, about 5 cm below the knee. Surrounding erythema extends approximately 3–4 cm beyond the wound; area is warm and tender with mild induration. Small amount of purulent exudate on dressing. No fluctuance, crepitus, necrosis, bullae, or lymphangitic streaking."
      }
    },
